Here's a simple HTML and JavaScript example to create a colorful website based on your mock-up, with two real jokes:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f0f8ff;
            color: #333;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        h1 {
            color: #4682b4;
        }
        .joke-container {
            background-color: #fff;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
            margin: 20px auto;
            padding: 20px;
            width: 80%;
            max-width: 600px;
        }
        .joke-title {
            font-size: 1.5em;
            color: #8b4513;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }
        .joke-content {
            font-size: 1.2em;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .joke-punchline {
            font-style: italic;
            color: #2e8b57;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="joke-container">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <div class="joke-title">[Really funny joke 1]</div>
        <div class="joke-content">Why don't scientists trust atoms?</div>
        <div class="joke-punchline">Because they make up everything!</div>

        <div class="joke-title">[Same but joke 2]</div>
        <div class="joke-content">Why did the scarecrow win an award?</div>
        <div class="joke-punchline">Because he was outstanding in his field!</div>
    </div>

    <script>
        // Optional: Add some interactivity or enhancements
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
            console.log('Website loaded!');
        });
    </script>
</body

Here's a simple HTML and JavaScript example to create an interactive joke website:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        h1 {
            color: #333;
        }
        .joke-container {
            background-color: #fff;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }
        .joke-text {
            color: #555;
        }
        .reveal-button {
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border-radius: 5px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 16px;
            margin-top: 10px;
        }
        .reveal-button:hover {
            background-color: #45a049;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
    <div class="joke-container">
        <p class="joke-text">[Funny Joke]</p>
        <button class="reveal-button" onclick="revealJoke()">Push to reveal punchline</button>
    </div>

    <script>
        function revealJoke() {
            document.querySelector('.joke-text').textContent = "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!";
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a simple website with a joke that is revealed when a button is clicked. The joke is replaced with a real joke for demonstration. You can customize the joke and styling as needed.
